@@@!atrep

@@/ koine: the common dialect - the shared core of text
@@/ formatting sims that genre dialektoi (litogramma,
@@/ lexigramma, ...) inherit and that authors meet everywhere
@@/ with the same symbols. Extracted from litogramma; ships
@@/ with atrep as part of the standard library. The scope is
@@/ deliberately semantic and minimal: front matter, generic
@@/ section levels, inline formatting, quotations, lists,
@@/ the plain footnote, and references. Tables and figures are
@@/ deliberately absent - layout concepts belong to
@@/ specialized dialektoi; genre structure (parts, chapters,
@@/ verse, drama, entries, senses) belongs to the heirs.

@=== title
@= grammata =@
@"text title"@
@""
Required. Must be the first content element of a document,
standing alone as a paragraph. One per document.
""@
===@

@=== subtitle
@=_ grammata _=@
@"text subtitle"@
===@

@=== author
@=: grammata :=@
@"author name; one sim per author, each its own paragraph"@
===@

@=== editor
@=; grammata ;=@
@""
Editor name; one sim per editor. For works that have an editor
rather than an author (dictionaries, anthologies), or in
addition to authors when the editorial role is significant
(critical editions).
""@
@"editor name"@
===@

@=== section
@#[(taxis)] lemma
grammata
#@
@"section"@
===@

@=== subsection
@##[(taxis)] lemma
grammata
##@
@"subsection"@
@^(#)
===@

@=== subsubsection
@###[(taxis)] lemma
grammata
###@
@"subsubsection"@
@^(##)
===@

@=== run-in-heading
@#_ grammata _#@
@"run-in heading (milepost, outside the ToC hierarchy)"@
@""
Endo-simmere that must start a paragraph and must end with a
punctuation mark; paragraph text follows on the same line.
""@
===@

@=== section-break
@** grammata **@
@"section break (asterism / dinkus)"@
@""
TENTATIVE symbol. Stands alone as a paragraph; canonical
grammata is the literal three-asterisk asterism. A structural
separation within a chapter, typeset as a rule or ornament.
""@
===@

@=== emphasis
@/ grammata /@
@"emphasis (italic)"@
===@

@=== strong
@* grammata *@
@"strong (bold)"@
===@

@=== strong-emphasis
@*/ grammata /*@
@"strong emphasis (bold italic)"@
===@

@=== annotation
@, grammata ,@
@"semantic annotation carrier"@
@""
General-purpose inline span whose meaning is given by a genos
on the episim; a genos is expected, though genoses cannot be
formally required by a dialect definition.
""@
===@

@=== unordered-list
@--
grammata
--@
@"unordered list; grammata is a sequence of unordered-item"@
===@

@=== unordered-item
@-
grammata
-@
@"unordered list item"@
@^(--)
===@

@=== ordered-list
@..
grammata
..@
@""
Ordered list; grammata is a sequence of ordered-item. Item
taxes must be consistent (one ordinal category per list) and
sequential without skips; the list may start at any value.
""@
@"ordered list"@
===@

@=== ordered-item
@.-(taxis)
grammata
-.@
@"ordered list item"@
@""
TENTATIVE symbol (the plain period belongs to the ordinal
sim).
""@
@^(..)
===@

@=== definition-list
@::;
grammata
;::@
@"definition list; grammata is a sequence of definition-item"@
===@

@=== definition-item
@:: lemma
grammata
::@
@"definition list item; the lemma is the term being defined"@
@^(::;)
===@

@=== definition
@;
grammata
;@
@"a single definition within a definition-item"@
@^(::)
===@

@=== footnote
@^
grammata
^@
@"footnote definition; onymized on the episim, attached by deixis"@
===@

@=== blockquote
@"
grammata
"@ [hypograph]
@"block quotation; the hypograph is the attribution"@
===@

@=== quotation
@"" grammata ""@
@"inline quotation; genos-refinable (.said for speech)"@
@""
Added after the TEI stress test (tei-coverage.md gap 1): TEI
q/said in running prose had no litogramma counterpart.
""@
===@

@=== ref
@>(onym)
@"cross-reference to an onym; renders the target's lemma"@
===@

@=== link
@>< grammata ><@
@"hyperlink; the grammata is the displayed URL"@
@""
Hidden-href links (display text distinct from the URL) are
deferred pending F9.
""@
===@
